{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1096759-the-pack-pack-experiences-and-open-table","id":1096759,"title":"[The Pack] Pack Experiences and Open Table","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T09:15:49-07:00","id":1096759,"title":"[The Pack] Pack Experiences and Open Table","content":"I run <b>WtF</b> 2E chronicle with <a href=\"http://thealexandrian.net/wordpress/38643/roleplaying-games/open-table-manifesto\" target=\"_blank\">Open Table model </a>in mind. Players are slowly hammering their 'Pack as Character' and here I have a bit problem. To this day, each player got their Beats on separate instances - we DID NOT do Pack Beats. It's partially because I assume there will probably can be big rotations with Open Table game model. Am I getting it right that I can somehow run Pack Experience as average of Beats all players earned in the game? Like Mike got 4 Beats, Lucy 3 Beats and Brian 2 Beats, so the Pack will get 3 Pack Beats on it own?<br /> <br /> Also, do Pack Beats coming from going over or resolving Pack Aspirations or Pack Complications are give to each particular character that took part in the event? Or all characters in the Pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:08:45-07:00","id":1101573,"title":"","content":"45 views and no comment? No one can advise my on subject?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:54:51-07:00","id":1101622,"title":"","content":"They way I have it run in my game is I have a pack aspiration. I hand out pack beats for every character that played a role on bringing that aspiration to a close. For instance the Pack is having trouble with a local Private Investigator who is looking into to the mysterious activity surrounding the pack. The pack takes the Aspiration &quot;Deal with the PI&quot; for the pack.<br /> <br /> Now if the combat focused werewolf just heads over and murders him, I am only awarding one beat, even if the pack came along. Only one Werewolf was really significantly involved in bringing that aspiration to a close.<br /> <br /> Now if they use the full resources of the pack, I award more pack beats depending on how important each pack members contribution to resolving said problem is.<br /> <br /> It might be good to have a short term and long term pack aspiration for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T07:53:22-07:00","id":1101638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1096759-the-pack-pack-experiences-and-open-table#post1096759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run <b>WtF</b> 2E chronicle with <a href=\"http://thealexandrian.net/wordpress/38643/roleplaying-games/open-table-manifesto\" target=\"_blank\">Open Table model </a>in mind. Players are slowly hammering their 'Pack as Character' and here I have a bit problem. To this day, each player got their Beats on separate instances - we DID NOT do Pack Beats. It's partially because I assume there will probably can be big rotations with Open Table game model. Am I getting it right that I can somehow run Pack Experience as average of Beats all players earned in the game? Like Mike got 4 Beats, Lucy 3 Beats and Brian 2 Beats, so the Pack will get 3 Pack Beats on it own?<br /> <br /> Also, do Pack Beats coming from going over or resolving Pack Aspirations or Pack Complications are give to each particular character that took part in the event? Or all characters in the Pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would just use Group Beats anyway: even if one of my players misses a session they get the beats that were earned anyway. I'd do the average if you insist on playing it the other way though. I would award all Pack Members who were present during an Aspiration being fulfilled or a Complication being resolved the Pack Beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T13:20:33-07:00","id":1223985,"title":"","content":"Almost a year later I have a related problem with Pack as Character - In our Vikings Era game one of players took young boy as slave. <b>He asked me how to advance a boy and let him buy stats, since new slave is not doing anything really special in the plot?</b> Then I found those rules in the <b>Pack</b> book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Pack, p. 27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the chapter, divide the total pack Beats by the number of players (round down). Every player receives this many Beats for their Uratha characters, whether the werewolves appeared in the story or not. If using the Pack as Character optional rules, the pack also receives this number of Beats as described on p. 20. Additionally, any Wolf-Blooded or human members of the pack who appeared as primary characters also receive the same number of Beats; those who didn\u2019t appear receive half this many Beats.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller keeps a running total of these additional Beats (and Experiences), so packmates who rarely appear can advance with the pack. Wolf-Blooded use the same Experience costs as Uratha (Werewolf: The Forsaken, p. 84), whereas human supporting cast can improve a dice pool, or purchase a new one, for five Experiences, and may improve Willpower for six Experiences.<br /> <br /> With this system, the Uratha always advance at the same pace no matter which characters the players choose to focus on each session, whereas the Wolf-Blooded and humans must be active to \u2018keep up\u2019, but still gradually evolve and advance with the pack even when not the focus of the action.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>So am I getting it right - <i>every</i> Extended Pack member get's half of whole's Pack Beats per session, even if he do not show in the particular game?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}